a little light reading it's been a long time since we've seen girls lounging around in fancy

31
00:04:03,147 --> 00:04:09,727
underwear i can't even get shigure or sayuri to wear bathing suits ask me to again and i'll

32
00:04:09,727 --> 00:04:16,567
gouge your eyes out i guess i'd have to wear one if the lieutenant colonel ordered me to that is

33
00:04:16,567 --> 00:04:21,827
did you hear that current for the sake of morale tell her to fight the bathing suit

34
00:04:21,827 --> 00:04:29,847
will you shut up you're supposed to be checking for vampires oh yeah mito's keeping an eye out how can

35
00:04:29,847 --> 00:04:37,567
you be so useless current i finished scoping out the interior there are no signs that vampires have

36
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:45,147
been here hey mito question would you wear a swimsuit why are you asking me that well pervert

37
00:04:45,147 --> 00:04:52,787
gurin over here wants to know what your body looks like under that uniform what but i what kind of

38
00:04:52,787 --> 00:04:58,667
dirty things have you been talking about do you really want to know current look the troops have

39
00:04:58,667 --> 00:05:10,307
started to arrive don't ignore me

40
00:05:10,307 --> 00:05:28,747
Good morning.

41
00:05:30,687 --> 00:05:32,967
Whoa, Xinya, where'd you get a car like this?

42
00:05:33,127 --> 00:05:35,727
It was abandoned on the side of the road, so I hotwired it.

43
00:05:35,907 --> 00:05:36,507
Awesome, huh?

44
00:05:36,827 --> 00:05:39,647
It's perfect for an impractical major general like you.

45
00:05:40,307 --> 00:05:41,467
What are you doing here?

46
00:05:42,267 --> 00:05:44,127
Brother Curito told me about your mission.

47
00:05:44,607 --> 00:05:46,727
Sounds like you guys are sacrificial pawns.

48
00:05:47,087 --> 00:05:50,087
A hundred troops don't stand much of a chance against the vampire nobles.

49
00:05:50,407 --> 00:05:51,907
Those bloodsuckers are too powerful.

50
00:05:53,287 --> 00:05:57,867
So I figured, why not bring my impractical self here and see if I can help out?

51
00:05:58,347 --> 00:05:59,887
Okay, you can thank me now.

52
00:06:02,087 --> 00:06:03,267
You're such a moron.

53
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:08,527
Well, now we're definitely gonna be late.

54
00:06:08,527 --> 00:06:10,487
Um, do you think we'll get in trouble?

55
00:06:10,907 --> 00:06:13,707
If Garin's mad, I'll just tell him it was Shinawa and Mitsuba's fault.

56
00:06:13,947 --> 00:06:15,627
How dare you sell out your comrades?

57
00:06:16,047 --> 00:06:18,427
Comrades, my ass. You tried to leave me behind.

58
00:06:18,727 --> 00:06:20,907
Hey, we went back and picked you up eventually.

59
00:06:20,907 --> 00:06:26,707
We'll leave here at 0700 hours.

60
00:06:27,247 --> 00:06:29,627
Six hours later, we will arrive in Nagoya.

61
00:06:30,607 --> 00:06:34,127
The directives I hand out will cover specific strategic details.

62
00:06:35,127 --> 00:06:36,747
Oh, nice of you to show up!

63
00:06:36,747 --> 00:06:40,187
I'm surprised you didn't miss the entire war.

64
00:06:40,867 --> 00:06:44,607
Well, you see, sir, we have a really good excuse for being late.

65
00:06:44,767 --> 00:06:47,047
It's not like we stopped at the hot springs for a long luxurious bath.

66
00:06:47,047 --> 00:06:48,107
Don't make excuses!

67
00:06:49,107 --> 00:06:51,407
This mission isn't some childish game.

68
00:06:51,867 --> 00:06:53,727
If you can't follow orders, leave now!

69
00:06:53,727 --> 00:07:00,107
Damn kid, screwing around.

70
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:03,767
Sorry, Lieutenant Colonel.

71
00:07:04,147 --> 00:07:06,267
This is my fault. I take all the blame.

72
00:07:06,847 --> 00:07:07,247
You?

73
00:07:08,527 --> 00:07:12,307
We were late because I took it upon myself to fight the four horsemen of John.

74
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,587
Does that mean you're going to leave?

75
00:07:15,007 --> 00:07:16,767
No, sir. Please let me stay.

76
00:07:17,267 --> 00:07:19,147
I want to help destroy the vampires.

77
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:21,947
Fall in line with the others.

78
00:07:22,587 --> 00:07:25,607
Just know, you'll have to face severe punishment later.

79
00:07:26,427 --> 00:07:27,147
You know...

80
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:29,947
Listen to me carefully, everyone.

81
00:07:30,687 --> 00:07:33,587
During this mission, I won't tolerate any failures.

82
00:07:34,247 --> 00:07:36,627
Follow my orders to the letter and don't fool around.

83
00:07:37,867 --> 00:07:41,547
This mission will probably be the most dangerous you will ever have.

84
00:07:42,327 --> 00:07:43,527
Many of you will die.

85
00:07:44,587 --> 00:07:46,787
Remember, everyone here is family.

86
00:07:46,787 --> 00:07:50,487
That means those who fall in battle are our brothers and sisters.

87
00:07:51,327 --> 00:07:52,967
But they won't die in vain.

88
00:07:53,367 --> 00:07:55,367
Their sacrifices will ensure our success.

89
00:07:55,827 --> 00:07:56,587
Let me be clear.

90
00:07:56,887 --> 00:07:58,607
Our goal isn't to come back alive.

91
00:07:59,007 --> 00:08:00,687
It is to be victorious no matter what.

92
00:08:01,007 --> 00:08:02,127
Do you understand me?

93
00:08:04,127 --> 00:08:04,407
Yeah!

94
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:21,907
I just want to apologize.

95
00:08:22,707 --> 00:08:23,787
This was all my fault.

96
00:08:23,947 --> 00:08:24,927
Hey, don't sweat it.

97
00:08:25,327 --> 00:08:26,827
What's the worst that Gurren can do to me?

98
00:08:27,727 --> 00:08:29,447
You can take all the blame next time.

99
00:08:31,947 --> 00:08:34,127
Special private Yuichiro Hyakuya!

100
00:08:34,507 --> 00:08:35,287
We're waiting.

101
00:08:36,087 --> 00:08:36,407
Okay.

102
00:08:36,547 --> 00:08:37,967
It's time for me to get an earful.

103
00:08:38,467 --> 00:08:39,067
No, wait.

104
00:08:39,407 --> 00:08:40,907
Let me go in with you and explain.

105
00:08:41,507 --> 00:08:41,767
Yeah.

106
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:43,947
And I was screwing around on the road, too.

107
00:08:44,287 --> 00:08:45,047
I'll tell Gurren.

108
00:08:45,527 --> 00:08:49,027
Well, if this is a party, I guess I might as well come for backup.

109
00:08:49,267 --> 00:08:50,227
Yeah, me too.

110
00:08:50,987 --> 00:08:52,567
Nah, don't worry about it, guys.

111
00:08:52,727 --> 00:08:54,647
I'm kind of used to Gurren yelling at me anyway.

112
00:08:56,087 --> 00:08:56,907
But you...

113
00:08:56,907 --> 00:09:10,827
Lieutenant Colonel Gurren.

114
00:09:11,147 --> 00:09:11,747
He's here.

115
00:09:17,387 --> 00:09:18,767
Hey, idiot you.

116
00:09:19,027 --> 00:09:19,667
How's it going?

117
00:09:20,547 --> 00:09:20,807
Huh?

118
00:09:21,307 --> 00:09:24,787
Why would you ask me a question like that when you're getting ready to lecture me?

119
00:09:24,787 --> 00:09:27,147
But none of this was your fault, was it?

120
00:09:27,627 --> 00:09:29,047
Uh, well...

121
00:09:29,047 --> 00:09:31,247
Taking the heat for your comrades is admirable.

122
00:09:31,707 --> 00:09:32,307
So what?

123
00:09:32,407 --> 00:09:33,827
You brought me here to reward me?

124
00:09:34,307 --> 00:09:35,667
Oh, now you understand.

125
00:09:36,067 --> 00:09:38,327
Our Gurren here is actually a big softie.

126
00:09:38,727 --> 00:09:39,007
Huh?

127
00:09:40,027 --> 00:09:40,827
Hey, wait!

128
00:09:41,027 --> 00:09:43,287
You're that guy from that place I had to go that time.

129
00:09:44,007 --> 00:09:46,527
You certainly don't have a gift for words, but you're right.

130
00:09:46,707 --> 00:09:47,387
Good to see you.

131
00:09:47,687 --> 00:09:48,327
That's enough.

132
00:09:48,407 --> 00:09:49,427
We're wasting time here.

133
00:09:49,727 --> 00:09:50,847
Goshi, let's get started.

134
00:09:51,527 --> 00:09:52,187
Yeah, yeah.

135
00:09:52,187 --> 00:09:54,187
Ew!

136
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:07,967
Ew!

137
00:10:08,327 --> 00:10:09,467
Hot, hot, very hot!

138
00:10:09,647 --> 00:10:10,967
I'm burning alive, you bastard!

139
00:10:11,907 --> 00:10:13,487
Come on, get me down from here!

140
00:10:13,667 --> 00:10:13,887
What?

141
00:10:14,367 --> 00:10:14,627
Whoa!

142
00:10:14,847 --> 00:10:15,627
No, no, no, no, no!

143
00:10:15,627 --> 00:10:15,927
Hey!

144
00:10:15,927 --> 00:10:19,927
An illusion spell?

145
00:10:20,827 --> 00:10:23,667
What kind of sick joke are you trying to pull, Gurren?

146
00:10:24,487 --> 00:10:25,407
It's no joke.

147
00:10:25,507 --> 00:10:26,987
This is your punishment, Shinoa.

148
00:10:29,127 --> 00:10:31,507
This is what you get for not fessing up yourself.

149
00:10:32,307 --> 00:10:36,407
I'm here to show you that not following orders can easily get your comrades killed.

150
00:10:37,207 --> 00:10:38,347
Yes, I know that.

151
00:10:38,587 --> 00:10:40,687
And I'm well aware that what I did was wrong.

152
00:10:40,827 --> 00:10:41,867
That's not good enough.

153
00:10:43,207 --> 00:10:46,567
You've never experienced what it's like to truly care for another person.

154
00:10:47,027 --> 00:10:49,527
And therefore, you don't understand the fear of losing someone.

155
00:10:49,527 --> 00:10:52,987
But from now on, things are different.

156
00:10:53,647 --> 00:10:55,627
One wrong move could get your comrades killed.

157
00:10:56,227 --> 00:10:58,647
As team leader, their lives are in your hands.

158
00:10:59,087 --> 00:11:00,147
I said I know that.

159
00:11:00,167 --> 00:11:01,687
And I said that's not enough, brat.

160
00:11:02,007 --> 00:11:02,407
Remember?

161
00:11:03,327 --> 00:11:04,587
Let me ask you something.

162
00:11:05,107 --> 00:11:07,967
What would you do if a huge threat suddenly appeared right now?

163
00:11:08,687 --> 00:11:10,287
Would you be able to manage your team?

164
00:11:10,287 --> 00:11:13,187
Right, let's see.

165
00:11:13,527 --> 00:11:17,087
A little test pitting me, Mito, and Shinya against you and your squad.

166
00:11:18,667 --> 00:11:20,567
The fight begins in ten seconds.

167
00:11:21,087 --> 00:11:21,387
Ten.

168
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:22,647
Nine.

169
00:11:22,807 --> 00:11:23,087
What?

170
00:11:23,247 --> 00:11:23,427
Eight.

171
00:11:23,427 --> 00:11:24,847
You seriously want us to fight?

172
00:11:25,067 --> 00:11:25,187
Seven.

173
00:11:25,187 --> 00:11:25,587
Six.

174
00:11:26,027 --> 00:11:26,267
Five.

175
00:11:26,267 --> 00:11:28,207
Come on, we need to put some distance between us and them.

176
00:11:28,207 --> 00:11:28,407
Three.

177
00:11:30,247 --> 00:11:30,687
Hmm.

178
00:11:31,367 --> 00:11:33,007
You shouldn't be so tough on Shinoa.

179
00:11:33,387 --> 00:11:35,187
You know she's trying really hard.

180
00:11:35,587 --> 00:11:36,727
That's awfully sweet of you.

181
00:11:36,727 --> 00:11:40,787
Why don't you show her your support by beating us instead of standing here looking stupid?

182
00:11:41,627 --> 00:11:43,747
Okay, but don't blame me when I embarrass you.

183
00:11:44,767 --> 00:11:46,507
Like I'd lose to some kid.

184
00:11:58,787 --> 00:12:01,627
First, I want to put the long-range fighters up against each other.

185
00:12:01,967 --> 00:12:04,167
That's Yoichi versus Major General Shinya.

186
00:12:04,387 --> 00:12:04,847
Got it.

187
00:12:04,847 --> 00:12:09,867
Based on what I know about Colonel Jujo, Mitsu and I should be able to hold her off.

188
00:12:10,807 --> 00:12:12,787
So our only real problem is Gurin?

189
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:13,527
Yes.

190
00:12:14,007 --> 00:12:16,707
The lieutenant colonel is a master of close quarters combat.

191
00:12:16,947 --> 00:12:18,467
Kimizuki and you will team up.

192
00:12:18,467 --> 00:12:22,247
If he manages to beat you two, then this test is as good as over.

193
00:12:22,787 --> 00:12:24,747
No sweat, we just have to take him down.

194
00:12:25,287 --> 00:12:27,787
Yeah, I've been waiting to get a piece of that loser.

195
00:12:28,567 --> 00:12:30,267
All right, take your positions.

196
00:12:34,847 --> 00:12:36,047
Okay, kids.

197
00:12:36,407 --> 00:12:37,287
Here we come.

198
00:12:43,227 --> 00:12:45,187
Shinya, allow me.

199
00:12:48,067 --> 00:12:49,547
Come on, Byakomaru.

200
00:12:49,967 --> 00:12:50,547
Get them.

201
00:12:50,547 --> 00:13:04,907
They're formation is already falling apart.

202
00:13:07,007 --> 00:13:08,287
Everyone, regroup.

203
00:13:08,627 --> 00:13:09,707
I'll cover our backs.

204
00:13:09,707 --> 00:13:17,747
You're not getting away, rookie.

205
00:13:23,567 --> 00:13:24,507
Let's do this.

206
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:26,467
I won't let you pass me, Gurin!

207
00:13:26,767 --> 00:13:27,587
You're an idiot.

208
00:13:27,587 --> 00:13:33,347
Hey, you're not half bad.

209
00:13:34,347 --> 00:13:35,027
Of course!

210
00:13:41,447 --> 00:13:42,947
The fight is over, children.

211
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:58,907
Come on, Gurin.

212
00:13:58,967 --> 00:14:00,147
Was that really necessary?

213
00:14:00,547 --> 00:14:01,747
Try not to cry.

214
00:14:02,447 --> 00:14:03,927
I'm not done with you!

215
00:14:08,587 --> 00:14:09,267
That's it!

216
00:14:09,547 --> 00:14:11,687
Everyone get into formation with you in the center!

217
00:14:11,687 --> 00:14:15,487
Whoa, Lieutenant Colonel Gurin is fighting those newbies.

218
00:14:15,687 --> 00:14:17,907
This must be some kind of punishment for being late.

219
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:20,007
Wow, look at that kid.

220
00:14:20,267 --> 00:14:23,387
Yeah, he's matching with the Lieutenant Colonel's attacks pretty well.

221
00:14:23,667 --> 00:14:25,927
There's no way the kid will beat him with power alone.

222
00:14:31,647 --> 00:14:36,727
What the hell?

223
00:14:37,367 --> 00:14:38,747
It's an explosion spell.

224
00:14:38,747 --> 00:14:40,127
Let me disenchant it.

225
00:14:41,687 --> 00:14:43,027
Not a chance.

226
00:14:44,687 --> 00:14:47,907
Now's the time to admit defeat before I blow your head off.

227
00:14:51,167 --> 00:14:53,647
If I explode, then I'm taking you with me!

228
00:14:53,887 --> 00:14:55,007
Whoa, no, I'm terrified.

229
00:14:55,687 --> 00:14:56,527
I'm just kidding.

230
00:14:56,947 --> 00:14:58,287
I figured you'd try something.

231
00:14:58,287 --> 00:15:05,467
There, I'm past your defenses.

232
00:15:06,087 --> 00:15:08,707
That means all your comrades are dead now.

233
00:15:10,767 --> 00:15:11,307
Damn it!

234
00:15:13,507 --> 00:15:13,927
You!

235
00:15:16,587 --> 00:15:18,067
I'll stop you!

236
00:15:18,067 --> 00:15:30,067
You should never challenge someone who is stronger than you are.

237
00:15:30,067 --> 00:15:33,647
And you guys are way too late.

238
00:15:35,407 --> 00:15:35,887
Stupid!

239
00:15:37,967 --> 00:15:39,007
What a disappointment.

240
00:15:39,867 --> 00:15:43,247
You've got three Black Demon holders in your squad, and this is the best you can do?

241
00:15:43,727 --> 00:15:46,327
The nobles are stronger than we are, and they won't hold back.

242
00:15:46,327 --> 00:15:49,127
Do you really think you stand a chance against them?

243
00:15:49,127 --> 00:15:52,167
All right.

244
00:15:52,907 --> 00:15:55,347
As you can see, these rookies need a lot of help.

245
00:15:55,927 --> 00:15:58,787
We're gonna have to show them what it means to be good comrades.

246
00:15:59,587 --> 00:16:02,427
Are we totally sure those three guys have Black Demon weapons?

247
00:16:02,727 --> 00:16:03,967
How'd they manage the trials?

248
00:16:04,387 --> 00:16:05,487
The weapons don't matter.

249
00:16:05,647 --> 00:16:07,227
Without teamwork, they're all useless.

250
00:16:07,727 --> 00:16:09,487
Guess that's why we gotta look after them.

251
00:16:09,487 --> 00:16:13,667
What's wrong? You look dissatisfied.

252
00:16:14,707 --> 00:16:15,247
I am.

253
00:16:15,567 --> 00:16:19,707
I'm thinking about what strategy we should use the next time we face off against your team.

254
00:16:20,067 --> 00:16:23,807
Oh, so the hot-headed little rebel has brains as well.

255
00:16:31,727 --> 00:16:33,147
Why are you touching me?

256
00:16:33,467 --> 00:16:35,167
This test pointed out your weaknesses.

257
00:16:36,007 --> 00:16:37,107
Focus on your teamwork.

258
00:16:37,107 --> 00:16:40,227
Excuse me. May I speak freely, sir?

259
00:16:42,267 --> 00:16:43,707
These kids are dangerous.

260
00:16:44,267 --> 00:16:45,847
Newbies have no place on the battlefield.

261
00:16:46,607 --> 00:16:50,167
They don't follow orders or obey rules, and they have no sense of teamwork.

262
00:16:50,507 --> 00:16:52,487
If you let them join us, they'll only drag us down.

263
00:16:52,967 --> 00:16:55,987
Hmm. Those are all problems, but how do we fix them?

264
00:16:56,967 --> 00:16:58,007
Oh, wait. I know.

265
00:16:58,527 --> 00:17:00,627
I'm putting your team in charge of them.

266
00:17:02,307 --> 00:17:04,727
Shikure, rearrange the team rosters.

267
00:17:04,727 --> 00:17:07,467
I want Shinoa's squad to join up with Narubis.

268
00:17:07,847 --> 00:17:08,407
Yes, sir.

269
00:17:08,847 --> 00:17:10,867
Wait. Please rethink this, Lieutenant Colonel.

270
00:17:11,007 --> 00:17:12,887
This is Sergeant Makoto Narubi.

271
00:17:13,967 --> 00:17:19,687
And that's Rika Inoue, Taro Kageyama, Yayoi Endo, and Chusaku Iwasaki.

272
00:17:20,387 --> 00:17:21,647
They're an excellent squad.

273
00:17:21,987 --> 00:17:22,947
They'll train you well.

274
00:17:23,467 --> 00:17:25,287
They don't seem too thrilled to have us.

275
00:17:25,387 --> 00:17:26,087
Please, sir.

276
00:17:26,087 --> 00:17:29,947
Listen up. Playtime's over, so let's focus. We've got a mission.

277
00:17:30,307 --> 00:17:30,747
Sir!

278
00:17:33,447 --> 00:17:35,307
I'm looking forward to serving with you.

279
00:17:35,307 --> 00:17:50,687
Thanks. You had to go and open your big mouth, didn't you?

280
00:17:50,747 --> 00:17:52,407
Do you realize how much work this is?

281
00:17:52,647 --> 00:17:54,647
Well, they do seem to have a lot of raw power.

282
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:57,207
With a little training, maybe they'll turn out to be useful.

283
00:17:57,207 --> 00:18:01,027
What's with that sergeant?

284
00:18:01,307 --> 00:18:02,367
You can't really blame him.

285
00:18:02,927 --> 00:18:05,607
He may be a complete jerk-off, but he's dead right about us.

286
00:18:06,607 --> 00:18:08,087
Hey, everyone.

287
00:18:09,767 --> 00:18:11,947
I'm sorry about how things turned out.

288
00:18:12,427 --> 00:18:13,927
All of this stuff is my fault.

289
00:18:14,847 --> 00:18:16,207
Not just being late.

290
00:18:16,447 --> 00:18:18,147
We lost because I'm incompetent.

291
00:18:19,187 --> 00:18:21,427
I don't think I'm fit to be called the commander.

292
00:18:21,427 --> 00:18:22,367
Don't say that.

293
00:18:22,647 --> 00:18:24,187
Did you not hear what Gurren said?

294
00:18:24,427 --> 00:18:26,387
All we need to do is learn to work as a team.

295
00:18:26,827 --> 00:18:28,707
And the first step is supporting each other.

296
00:18:29,787 --> 00:18:30,787
We're a family.

297
00:18:31,387 --> 00:18:33,547
The more we work together, the stronger we'll be.

298
00:18:33,927 --> 00:18:34,247
Yeah.

299
00:18:34,707 --> 00:18:36,367
And that means we still need a commander.

300
00:18:38,207 --> 00:18:40,227
So what do you think, Shinawa?

301
00:18:42,067 --> 00:18:42,507
Okay.

302
00:18:51,427 --> 00:18:55,547
Vampires!

303
00:18:55,647 --> 00:18:56,227
Vampires are coming!

304
00:19:01,867 --> 00:19:02,407
Vampires!

305
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:07,987
Vampires!

306
00:19:12,827 --> 00:19:13,307
Vampires!

307
00:19:19,047 --> 00:19:20,047
Vampires!

308
00:19:20,687 --> 00:19:21,127
Vampires!

309
00:19:21,127 --> 00:19:25,127
No! Please don't hurt me!

310
00:19:51,127 --> 00:19:57,127
They're gifts for the nobles in Nagoya.

311
00:19:57,127 --> 00:20:00,127
If you want to take a little sip, now's the time, Mika.

312
00:20:00,127 --> 00:20:03,127
I'm not interested in drinking human blood.

313
00:20:03,127 --> 00:20:05,127
Wait, is that some kind of joke?

314
00:20:05,127 --> 00:20:07,127
If you're afraid of getting caught, don't worry.

315
00:20:07,127 --> 00:20:10,127
You can trust me. I won't tell a soul.

316
00:20:12,127 --> 00:20:14,127
What a weirdo.

317
00:20:21,127 --> 00:20:39,127
The day will come when you will have to drink from a human.

318
00:20:39,127 --> 00:20:54,127
No! Stop! Please! I'm not going with you!

319
00:21:09,127 --> 00:21:19,127
See there? I knew you looked thirsty.

320
00:21:33,127 --> 00:21:35,127
Yes, definitely a weirdo.

321
00:21:39,127 --> 00:21:41,127
There is no warning.

322
00:21:41,127 --> 00:21:43,127
Teach him to make meteor.

323
00:21:43,127 --> 00:21:44,127
The Goat.

324
00:21:44,127 --> 00:21:46,127
The Goat is still up.

325
00:21:46,127 --> 00:22:16,107
We'll be right back.

326
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:34,887
Next time on Seraph of the End, Livestock Revolt.

